The base rate is 0%: The FDA has never approved psilocybin for any indication. But the evidence base is maturing. In June and July 2025, COMPASS Pathways’ COMP360 hit the primary endpoint in its first Phase 3 TRD trial and the company subsequently said, after a “positive” FDA meeting, it would accelerate launch plans by 9–12 months and pursue a rolling submission, making a late-2026 decision window at least plausible if the second pivotal readout is supportive.&#x20;

FDA psychedelic-trial guidance (2023) and NIH overview confirm the pathway exists but is demanding. [FDA Issues First Draft Guidance on Clinical Trials with Psychedelic Drugs | FDA](https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-issues-first-draft-guidance-clinical-trials-psychedelic-drugs)

Countervailing signals: FDA’s treatment of MDMA (where we saw harsh advisory committee votes and a subsequent reset) shows the agency’s high bar on psychedelic therapies and trial conduct, which could slow or complicate psilocybin review even with positive data.

A second late-stage program (Usona, MDD) is also in Phase 3, but its timing looks farther out, reducing the number of near-term shots on goal in 2026.&#x20;

What would move me up: a clearly positive second pivotal COMP360 readout and news that FDA accepted/started a priority review in early 2026.

What would move me down: FDA feedback flagging trial-quality or safety issues, or company guidance slipping an NDA beyond mid-2026.
